ith Table 8 type shares (each word share at most its type share, type union at most the sum of word shares) and inspected the x-axis ticks.","status":"linked_finding","reason":"Bar values are consistent with Table 8 and the text, but the axis labels 2% and 8% sit at 2.5% and 7.5% (NUM-006).","finding_ids":["NUM-006"],"attempted":true,"importance":"central","scope":"exhaustive"},{"item_id":"display:OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798","source_object_ids":["OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798"],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Inspected figure_3.png and compared the 35%, 44% and 9 pp statements and the 2024 gap wording with Appendix A.1.","status":"linked_finding","reason":"The 9 pp arithmetic holds, but the 2024 gap wording and the end-of-period quarter base are not reconciled (NUM-003, NUM-004).","finding_ids":["NUM-003","NUM-004"],"attempted":true,"importance":"peripheral","scope":"exhaustive"},{"item_id":"display:OBJ-d491066348ee1a73c8bce8f5","source_object_ids":["OBJ-d491066348ee1a73c8bce8f5"],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Compared county shares in the text (61, 52, 38, 14, 13, 7 percent) with the Figure 4 values and tested that 38.1% lies between the county minimum and maximum.","status":"checked_no_issue","reason":"Text values match Figure 4 within rounding. The weighted national average cannot be tested because county listing counts and the dashed-line value are not given.","finding_ids":[],"attempted":true,"importance":"peripheral","scope":"exhaustive"},{"item_id":"display:OBJ-8ec9459ce44d02c62d0a27bf","source_object_ids":["OBJ-8ec9459ce44d02c62d0a27bf"],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Read Table 1 from the page 5 text and compared its numeric examples (4 articles in 2 newspapers, 3 km, 3.5 m) with the rest of the paper.","status":"checked_no_issue","reason":"Table 1 holds mainly descriptive field definitions. The only quantities are illustrative examples consistent with Table 2 and the text.","finding_ids":[],"attempted":true,"importance":"central","scope":"exhaustive"},